      "description": "As the claim acknowledges, Lean replaces (4), the assertion of ¬B(⊥), with a proof in T of B(σ) → σ for each sentence σ. The σ = ⊥ instance is equivalent to (4); the other instances are additional premises. This is a schema, not a single assertion in T that all its beliefs are true."
